@style(IDocDemo)
@title(Charts: Relationships)

Scatter, error bars, bubbles, heatmaps, radar, polar and networks. Each chart is followed by the source that drew it, and every example carries its own data.

@table(widths=equal)
@row
@cell
@b{Scatter}

Two columns against each other. Add `trend=` for a fit and its R².

@graph(type=scatter, x=voltage, y=current, trend=linear, showR2, title="Ohm's law")
@data
voltage,current
1,0.10
2,0.19
3,0.31
4,0.39
5,0.52
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=scatter, x=voltage, y=current, trend=linear, showR2, title="Ohm's law")
@data
voltage,current
1,0.10
2,0.19
3,0.31
4,0.39
5,0.52
@end
@end
@endcell
@cell
@b{Error bars}

Measurements with their uncertainty. `yerr=` names the ± column; it also works on a line or scatter.

@graph(type=error_bar, x=trial, y=mean, yerr=sd, title="Reaction time (ms)")
@data
trial,mean,sd
1,312,24
2,298,19
3,281,22
4,276,15
5,270,12
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=error_bar, x=trial, y=mean, yerr=sd, title="Reaction time (ms)")
@data
trial,mean,sd
1,312,24
2,298,19
3,281,22
4,276,15
5,270,12
@end
@end
@endcell
@endtable

@table(widths=equal)
@row
@cell
@b{Bubble}

Scatter with a third column as size — and a fourth as time, animated.

@graph(type=bubble, x=income, y=life, size=pop, label=country, title="Gapminder")
@data
country,income,life,pop
Norway,64800,82.4,5.4
India,6400,69.7,1380
Brazil,14100,75.9,212
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=bubble, x=income, y=life, size=pop, label=country, title="Gapminder")
@data
country,income,life,pop
Norway,64800,82.4,5.4
India,6400,69.7,1380
Brazil,14100,75.9,212
@end
@end

Add `time=year` and a year column to animate it — press play or drag the scrubber.
@endcell
@cell
@b{Heatmap}

A grid coloured by value — two categories and a number.

@graph(type=heatmap, x=hour, y=day, value=n, title="When people submit")
@data
day,hour,n
Mon,09:00,3
Mon,17:00,8
Mon,23:00,14
Tue,09:00,5
Tue,17:00,6
Tue,23:00,11
Wed,09:00,4
Wed,17:00,9
Wed,23:00,16
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=heatmap, x=hour, y=day, value=n, title="When people submit")
@data
day,hour,n
Mon,09:00,3
Mon,17:00,8
Mon,23:00,14
Tue,09:00,5
Tue,17:00,6
Tue,23:00,11
Wed,09:00,4
Wed,17:00,9
Wed,23:00,16
@end
@end
@endcell
@endtable

@table(widths=equal)
@row
@cell
@b{Radar}

Several measures on one shape — profiles compared.

@graph(type=radar, label=skill, value=score, title="Rubric")
@data
skill,score
Correctness,4
Clarity,3
Efficiency,5
Style,4
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=radar, label=skill, value=score, title="Rubric")
@data
skill,score
Correctness,4
Clarity,3
Efficiency,5
Style,4
@end
@end
@endcell
@cell
@b{Polar}

Angle and radius — anything cyclic (wind, phase, time of day).

@graph(type=polar, x=angle, y=r, title="Antenna pattern")
@data
angle,r
0,1.0
45,0.7
90,0.2
135,0.7
180,1.0
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=polar, x=angle, y=r, title="Antenna pattern")
@data
angle,r
0,1.0
45,0.7
90,0.2
135,0.7
180,1.0
@end
@end
@endcell
@endtable


@table(widths=equal)
@row
@cell
@b{Network}

Things and the links between them. An edge list is enough; hover a node to see what it touches, drag it, click to pin. `dict` draws the equation dictionary itself.

@graph(type=network, mark=Calculus)
@data
source,target,group
Calculus,Physics,math
Calculus,Statistics,math
Linear algebra,Statistics,math
Linear algebra,Machine learning,math
Statistics,Machine learning,data
Physics,Engineering,science
Calculus,Engineering,math
@end

@code(idoc)
@graph(type=network, mark=Calculus)
@data
source,target,group
Calculus,Physics,math
Calculus,Statistics,math
Linear algebra,Statistics,math
Linear algebra,Machine learning,math
Statistics,Machine learning,data
Physics,Engineering,science
Calculus,Engineering,math
@end
@end
@endcell
@cell
@endcell
@endtable
